-- How `l4 render` shows a value the type checker added from a TYPICALLY
-- default. The same value is written out in a twin of each rule, so a test can
-- put the two renderings side by side: a rendered document is read by someone
-- who never sees the source, and the two must not read alike.

GIVEN rate IS A NUMBER TYPICALLY 3
      base IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
scaled MEANS rate TIMES base

GIVEN fee  IS A NUMBER TYPICALLY 12500
      base IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`big fee` MEANS fee PLUS base

DECLARE Colour IS ONE OF Red, Green

GIVEN colour IS A Colour TYPICALLY Green
      urgent IS A BOOLEAN TYPICALLY FALSE
      base   IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
graded MEANS IF urgent THEN base ELSE base

-- A call that is a rule's whole body renders as a field list.
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the bill` MEANS scaled WITH base IS n

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the written bill` MEANS scaled WITH base IS n, rate IS 3

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the big bill` MEANS `big fee` WITH base IS n

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the graded bill` MEANS graded WITH base IS n

-- A call inside a larger expression renders as a sentence.
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the nested bill` MEANS IF n EQUALS 0 THEN 0 ELSE scaled WITH base IS n

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the nested big bill` MEANS IF n EQUALS 0 THEN 0 ELSE `big fee` WITH base IS n

-- A record construction renders as a field list.
DECLARE Paint HAS
  coats  IS A NUMBER
  colour IS A STRING TYPICALLY "red"

`some paint` MEANS Paint WITH coats IS 2

`some written paint` MEANS Paint WITH coats IS 2, colour IS "red"

-- A list of record constructions renders as a table. One column holds a
-- default in the first row and a value the author wrote in the second.
GIVETH A LIST OF Paint
`all paints` MEANS LIST (Paint WITH coats IS 1), (Paint WITH coats IS 2, colour IS "blue")
